plied by the School of Computing website; this does not assign the paper to that school.","image","projectMedia","Creator project media","SolarRenderer authors · model output","Source reviewed","2026-10-18","verified","Year","2026","year","list","Tracks","ordered",false,[191,192,92],"dimensions","2D","3D","Development stages",[196,197,92],"stages","Gameplay & code","Engines & scenes","Topics",[201,202,203,204,205,206],"tags","hybrid-renderer","structure-conditioning","streaming","MiniMax-H3","LoRA","released-code","Further reading",[209,210,211,212,213],{"_51":222,"_27":223},{"_51":220,"_27":221},{"_51":218,"_27":219},{"_51":216,"_27":217},{"_51":214,"_27":215},"Usage guide","https://github.com/Junchao-cs/SolarWM/blob/main/docs/solar_renderer.md","Data and evaluation","https://huggingface.co/datasets/Enderfga/SolarRenderer-Data","Weights","https://huggingface.co/Enderfga/SolarRenderer","Paper PDF","https://enderfga.cn/data/solarrenderer.pdf","Code","https://github.com/Enderfga/SolarRenderer","Project source",[226],{"_51":224,"_27":70},"Why it belongs here","Few-Step Generative Reference Rendering conditions MiniMax-H3 on semantic maps, grayboxes, skeletons, depth, and other structures, with an optional first frame and text. Control and four-step LoRAs include a block-causal variant. Code is Apache-2.0; weights use the geographically restricted MiniMax H3 Community License, and data has component-specific terms, including noncommercial and research-only portions. Upstream programs must maintain world state and rules. Four-step sampling alone does not establish real-time consumer-hardware interaction.","detail","Resource type","Paper","Category","category","summary","name","paper",[246,247,248,249,250],[201,202,203,204,205,206],[244,245,109],[242,243,109],2026,"2d","3d","code","scene",{"_51":222,"_27":223},{"_51":220,"_27":221},{"_51":218,"_27":219},{"_51":216,"_27":217},{"_51":214,"_27":215},{"_252":253},"documents",{"_254":255,"_256":257},"en",[259,263,264,265,262,2